#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128996 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129177 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "a6d910ae-c6db-51d2-93ba-f6c823c0a8c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-6179" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z= x^2 + xy$ at the point $(1,2, 3).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = (x-x_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0) + (y-y_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =2x+y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y) = (1,2)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2) & =2(1)+2=4 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-3 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) \\\\ z-3 & =4(x-1)+1(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =4x+y-6 \\\\ -4x-y+z+3 & =0 \\\\ 4x+y-z-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128997 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129178 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points at Which Tangent Planes Have Particular Properties"}] :question/id #uuid "4eb4806c-3d5b-5ed2-87a1-d1ed50c267e5" :question/math-academy-id "e-6182" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z={y^2}+ {xy}$  is the tangent plane horizontal?" :question/worked-solution "The tangent plane to a surface is horizontal if and only if the normal vector to the tangent plane is vertical. So, let's first find the general expression of a normal vector to the surface.\n\nRemember that the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = (x-x_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0) + (y-y_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\left\\langle \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0), \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0), -1 \\right\\rangle$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =2y+x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n\\left\\langle y, \\: 2y+x, \\: -1 \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe want to find where this normal vector is vertical. This means that the $x$- and $y$-components of the vector must be $0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/df/df6542baabd72b24ce115cb79c912c7b19fd3bd1b663467956445553b60a68c1.png) \n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2(0) +x = 0 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x = 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=0$ and $y=0$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz = 0^2+(0)(0)= 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point where the tangent plane is horizontal is $(0,0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128999 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129180 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/id #uuid "ed1a3960-c2c4-57e7-8fd1-daf5d98bf052" :question/math-academy-id "e-6185" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=x^2+y^2+z^2-2xyz$ at the point $(1,-1,1,5).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $(x_0, y_0, z_0,w_0)$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw - w_0 = (x-x_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0,z_0) + (y-y_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0,z_0) + (z-z_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}(x_0,y_0,z_0).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2xyz)=2x-2yz \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2xyz)=2y-2xz \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2xyz)=2z-2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z) = (1,-1,1)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1) & =2(1)-2(-1)(1)=4 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1) & =2(-1)-2(1)(1)=-4 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) & =2(1)-2(1)(-1)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-5 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1)+(y+1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting and simplifying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-5 & =4(x-1)-4(y+1)+4(z-1) \\\\ w-5 & =4x-4y+4z-12 \\\\ -4x+4y-4z+w+7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-4y+4z-w-7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129177 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bb366f1-12dc-5aee-9d35-764f104afbf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383120} {:answer/id #uuid "94e574ae-07ac-5eb6-b3d2-c51cddbcb045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383121} {:answer/id #uuid "fb950b0d-2160-5039-8069-6f1037f3b3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383122} {:answer/id #uuid "595ffa56-42c9-52bf-ac03-04f1b4b665c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383123} {:answer/id #uuid "998e9a1e-f23f-589e-9d15-2fb4cb59c627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y+z+6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94e574ae-07ac-5eb6-b3d2-c51cddbcb045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383121} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9e6f910-725b-50a0-a031-e08e5288c76c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "211a5df8-dc28-5105-9dc3-9a4bf9482552" :question/math-academy-id "q-129441" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)$ at the point $(0,-2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(0,-2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,-2) & =\\frac{2(0)(-2)}{{0}^{2}+1}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,-2) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({0}^{2}+1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-0 & =(x-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,-2)+(y-(-2))\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,-2) \\\\ z & =0x+0(y+2) \\\\ z & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129177 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "100c6709-40f5-5599-8f17-63d73399f24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-3y-3z+5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383134} {:answer/id #uuid "1a79b5c5-d9b3-5029-90e7-c97121bfdbf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y-3z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383135} {:answer/id #uuid "021038f2-72cf-5531-b952-8071f1388ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y+4z-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383136} {:answer/id #uuid "dc595fac-dae6-5410-827a-24f260bf76a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y-z+5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383137} {:answer/id #uuid "29783bfa-7d2c-50b4-9f47-577066578c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "021038f2-72cf-5531-b952-8071f1388ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y+4z-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383136} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad277999-1600-53ea-b3c5-8876cd3b2822" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "719dda21-a080-5a82-b20d-e82c1de432a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-129446" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=x\\sqrt{y}-y\\sqrt{x}$ at the point $(1,4,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{y}-y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\sqrt{y}-y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}}-\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(1,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,4) & =\\sqrt{4}-\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{1}}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,4) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}-\\sqrt{1}=-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-(-2) & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,4)+(y-4)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,4) \\\\ z+2 & =0(x-1)-\\frac{3}{4}(y-4) \\\\ z+2 & =-\\frac{3}{4}y+3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}y+z-1 & =0 \\\\ 3y+4z-4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129180 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5247603b-df0f-5af7-999b-22318a03bb24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y+4z+w+\\pi -2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263709} {:answer/id #uuid "6a42fc74-d4c0-5b0f-b144-d17c1439943d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+w+\\pi +1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263913} {:answer/id #uuid "83682e8f-1c78-5a74-a7d4-252076631ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x-2y-2z-w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264129} {:answer/id #uuid "a89d7e70-578b-518c-80b6-1f7f26a1098d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+\\pi z+w=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264440} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1f74f6-a8ea-5722-b156-ff94b24566b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y-w+\\pi +3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83682e8f-1c78-5a74-a7d4-252076631ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x-2y-2z-w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264129} :answer-field/id #uuid "a65d643e-318b-5eba-9f29-9c077a35ae96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1621000-820d-5620-bf58-3ce548df1dda" :question/math-academy-id "q-129485" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz)$ at the point $(-1,1,1,-\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz))=4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz))=\\frac{4xz}{1+{y}^{2}{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz))=\\frac{4xy}{1+{y}^{2}{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(-1,1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(-1,1,1) & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1\\cdot 1)=\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(-1,1,1) & =\\frac{4(-1)(1)}{1+({1}^{2})({1}^{2})}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(-1,1,1) & =\\frac{4(-1)(1)}{1+({1}^{2})({1}^{2})}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-(-\\pi ) & =(x-(-1))\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(-1,1,1)+(y-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(-1,1,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(-1,1,1) \\\\ w+\\pi  & =\\pi (x+1)-2(y-1)-2(z-1) \\\\ w+\\pi  & =\\pi x-2y-2z+4+\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x-2y-2z-w+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129610 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129177 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0caeec29-3446-59d6-929a-da0cd6def940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+4y-z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321249} {:answer/id #uuid "218b3d6e-723a-57b0-b05e-f5ef5d66c924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+6y-z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321400} {:answer/id #uuid "52bcf9a2-7660-5058-a7d1-f5e4ac1fb320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8x+3y-z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321799} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0d0dc7-0e7f-5b67-b3b1-975d12d46b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+4y-z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322249} {:answer/id #uuid "937cdd9e-46a7-5faa-9ab8-81f2619665b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+4y-z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0caeec29-3446-59d6-929a-da0cd6def940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+4y-z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321249} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eb1e71a-8aff-588b-b599-a3d0d8de5885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab92392f-12a1-569b-997c-793bd45fc373" :question/math-academy-id "q-37595" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z={y}^{2}{e}^{2x}-1$ at the point $(0,2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}{e}^{2x}-1) \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}{e}^{2x}-1) \\\\  & =2y{e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,2) & =2(2)^{2}{e}^{2(0)}=8 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,2) & =2(2){e}^{2(0)}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-3 & =(x-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,2) \\\\ z-3 & =8(x-0)+4(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =8x+4y-8 \\\\ -8x-4y+z+5 & =0 \\\\ 8x+4y-z-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129180 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7d36749-f475-597e-835a-78a446b9e487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + y - 3z - w - 1 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128624} {:answer/id #uuid "1003ac62-bbbc-5e6d-8bbc-713a0e671451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x + y + z - w - 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128625} {:answer/id #uuid "13c9a77b-8071-55b1-8688-0b5367f5d17c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - 3y + z - w - 2 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128626} {:answer/id #uuid "38e7b785-7cfc-5503-8f7d-498fc37232e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 3y + z - w - 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128627} {:answer/id #uuid "6b70bf94-ce51-5371-a3ed-aa5d383ae7e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x - y + z - w - 2 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128628}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5abfb549-718a-51d0-8312-0a6705ded8ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128623}] :question/id #uuid "4e585b01-67a5-5f57-8d63-4d988a271f9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73729" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w = x^{2} - y^{2} + xyz$ at the point $(1, 1, 1, 1)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129177 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7676133-ac7f-5840-b8d3-72e48bc381e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-7y+z-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385580} {:answer/id #uuid "62789625-0d13-5f3c-9713-b48b33e855fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7x+11y-z-30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385581} {:answer/id #uuid "28f3efb2-a8a3-5292-965f-156e973895f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-7y-z+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385582} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0114f8-20c1-562a-b2e7-a7011c766d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7x-11y+z+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385583} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf255fb-dec1-53cd-ad7d-7500bd87d32a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-7y+z+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28f3efb2-a8a3-5292-965f-156e973895f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-7y-z+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385582} :answer-field/id #uuid "16767eef-05e8-5044-bf02-09ec5aa40dc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfc70561-1a2a-5f2a-a99a-d351a4cfe338" :question/math-academy-id "q-73844" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z={x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3}$ at the point $(1,2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2xy \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =2xy+{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(1,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2) & =3(1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+2(1)(2)=11 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) & =2(1)(2)+{1}^{2}-3(2)^{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-(-1) & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) \\\\ z+1 & =11(x-1)-7(y-2) \\\\ z+1 & =11x-7y+3 \\\\ -11x+7y+z-2 & =0 \\\\ 11x-7y-z+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129180 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37e1eeb8-4189-5718-8f50-bdf2f86033b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+15y+16z-w-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435526} {:answer/id #uuid "7147124b-3c14-59fb-b95d-12d323b0e513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+15y+16z+w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435531} {:answer/id #uuid "df2eecc4-dc64-5c9b-8ab8-81624c44bb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-15y+16z+w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435541} {:answer/id #uuid "f3dc19b2-fcd8-593e-b5c7-c02d25ef9070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+15y-16z+w-6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435542} {:answer/id #uuid "f64cc117-a5b0-5386-a6c5-f6d385b6497f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-15y-16z+w+6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7147124b-3c14-59fb-b95d-12d323b0e513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+15y+16z+w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435531} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6aa0ef9-33dc-511a-a8b4-7535395d3236" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "923d3b9b-11dc-5749-a7e2-257ace8090ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-73849" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=2x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}z$ at the point $(2,-2,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}z)=2{y}^{2}-6xz \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}z)=4xy+{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}-3{x}^{2}z)=2yz-3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(2,-2,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,-2,1) & =2(-2)^{2}-6(2)(1)=-4 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,-2,1) & =4(2)(-2)+(1)^{2}=-15 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,-2,1) & =2(-2)(1)-3(2)^{2}=-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-2 & =(x-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,-2,1)+(y+2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,-2,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,-2,1) \\\\ w-2 & =-4(x-2)-15(y+2)-16(z-1) \\\\ w-2 & =-4x+8-15y-30-16z+16 \\\\ 4x+15y+16z+w+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129180 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf0dc93-d9d4-5f21-8930-dd5004fc42a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-2y-2z-w-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407507} {:answer/id #uuid "5110fa49-48ce-56a6-b93d-b9d08b07b745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+2y+2z-w-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407508} {:answer/id #uuid "728a521d-8a62-5203-8384-b89408abe64b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-2y-2z+w-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407509} {:answer/id #uuid "72b11d02-8ab8-5c20-a244-f44e993b6792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+2y-2z-w+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407510} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e8ca25-16b2-54a8-b96c-ad5665775b39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-2y+2z+w-8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cf0dc93-d9d4-5f21-8930-dd5004fc42a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-2y-2z-w-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407507} :answer-field/id #uuid "75cea473-3250-5a97-b3ad-a51baa102dcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ca7d6fc-55d0-503c-8138-64f03d668ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73850" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2})$ at the point $(1,-1,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}))=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}))=\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}))=-\\frac{2z}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1) & =\\frac{2(1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}-(1)^{2}}=2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1) & =\\frac{2(-1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}-(1)^{2}}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) & =-\\frac{2(1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}-(1)^{2}}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-0 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1)+(y+1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) \\\\ w & =2(x-1)-2(y+1)-2(z-1) \\\\ w & =2x-2-2y-2-2z+2 \\\\ -2x+2y+2z+w+2 & =0 \\\\ 2x-2y-2z-w-2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129178 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points at Which Tangent Planes Have Particular Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52002c6b-9859-5b7b-a1de-586418b14736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,3,28)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339881} {:answer/id #uuid "551d2228-56ee-5488-91bb-0169794e5cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-3,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339910} {:answer/id #uuid "796a4945-abaa-5bd2-997d-087f2262b1b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,3,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340210} {:answer/id #uuid "8a645bd4-5f4d-5164-aa70-44b211e15ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-3,0)$ and $(-1,3,28)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340364} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b33a5b-7afb-5095-9268-a98f89267aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-3,0)$ and $(3,1,20)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "551d2228-56ee-5488-91bb-0169794e5cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-3,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339910} :answer-field/id #uuid "e58edcff-ee66-5f0c-86cd-1ec279fff31c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c589653c-432a-5bb8-acb2-94698429fbb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-73857" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z={x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}+6y+10$ is the tangent plane horizontal?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}+6y+10) \\\\  & =2x-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}+6y+10) \\\\  & =2y+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨2x-2,\\,2y+6,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNote that the tangent plane is horizontal if and only if the normal vector is vertical. This means that the $x$- and $y$-components of the vector must be $0:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2x-2=0 \\\\ 2y+6=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=1$ while the second equation gives $y=-3.$ \n\nFinally, substituting $x=1$ and $y=-3$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz={1}^{2}-2(1)+(-3)^{2}+6(-3)+10=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point where the tangent plane is horizontal is $(1,-3,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129178 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points at Which Tangent Planes Have Particular Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90f4afcf-4af1-5320-a876-c7e43193b7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,-1,1)$ and $(1,-1,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403712} {:answer/id #uuid "aaeb48d9-f69d-5b9e-9626-640bfefc395e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-1,-3)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403713} {:answer/id #uuid "98696df4-b0fb-53ef-a177-bce372e2f606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,1,0)$ and $(-1,1,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403714} {:answer/id #uuid "1cffc4be-00ee-57b7-9ac9-95e61bc1ca5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-1,2)$ and $(-1,-1,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403715} {:answer/id #uuid "479f131a-35b5-598d-93be-4ae6e4b42f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,-1,1)$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90f4afcf-4af1-5320-a876-c7e43193b7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,-1,1)$ and $(1,-1,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403712} :answer-field/id #uuid "29a46a2f-b76d-5223-bfa0-caee05f36438" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14749651-a6a1-55fa-b209-fec427b8a368" :question/math-academy-id "q-73860" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z={x}^{3}-3x+{y}^{2}+2y$ is the tangent plane horizontal?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-3x+{y}^{2}+2y) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-3 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}-3x+{y}^{2}+2y) \\\\  & =2y+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨3{x}^{2}-3,\\,2y+2,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNote that the tangent plane is horizontal if and only if the normal vector is vertical. This means that the $x$- and $y$-components of the vector must be $0:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-3=0 \\\\ 2y+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=\\pm 1$ while the second equation gives $y=-1.$ \n\nFinally, substituting $x=-1$ and $y=-1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz=(-1)^{3}-3(-1)+(-1)^{2}+2(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1$ and $y=-1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz=(1)^{3}-3(1)+(-1)^{2}+2(-1)=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points where the tangent plane is horizontal are $(-1,-1,1)$ and $(1,-1,-3).$"}]}
